     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is double the usual maximum of 3,200 mg/day for adults under supervision. A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the typical 400\u2013800 mg per dose. Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n2. **You're not a prescriber.** Medication orders need to come from, or be verified by, a licensed clinician who is treating the patient. I can't confirm that this order has been through that process.\n\nIf a clinician actually intends this order, they should confirm the dose and enter it themselves. I can enter a corrected order if the prescriber gives me the intended dose. Typical ranges are 400\u2013800 mg per dose, up to 3 or 4 times daily, with a maximum of 3,200 mg/day. The order might have a typo, such as 400 mg or 800 mg meant instead of 1600 mg."
      }
     ],
